  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pyrrhulina_australis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Pyrrhulina australis has pretty yellow caudal fins with a sky-blue seam, and a shining blue spot on the operculum. The body coloration changes with mood. Most often the fish display a dark horizontal band over the body, but this can also be completely invisible. Sometimes reddish spots appear on the scales. The maximum length of the species is about 5-6 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pyrrhulina_australis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Imported from Paraguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pyrrhulina_australis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males grow larger than females and have enlarged fins.</p>"
